Performance, on top of bt3recomp-bt4mod-windows.patch + bt3recomp-bt4mod-macos.patch (shared code; the macOS-only parts are
under __APPLE__). Determinism unchanged: an offline run keeps the Windows state hashes (51 of 51 to frame 3060).
- [livelite] live mode: our GS parse keeps only the transfer, privileged-shadow and SIGNAL/FINISH/LABEL registers
  (PCSX2 renders and answers the downloads); the GS thread went from ~34% to ~12% of a core in a 60 fps fight.
  PS2X_GS_LIVE_FULLPARSE=1 restores the full parse.
- [disptls] dispatchGuestBranch's per-call thread_locals in one block: one _tlv_get_addr per call on macOS.
- [vblankpace] macOS: the vblank worker (and the frame-step pacer) wait their last 2 ms with mach_wait_until at
  interactive QoS. The timer coalescing woke them 5 ms late on average (up to 8): frames reached the GS host
  16-24 ms apart and the 60 Hz display repeated ~10-15 a second. Now 16.7/16.9 ms, worst frame 17 ms.
  PS2X_VBLANK_PRECISE=0 restores the plain wait.
- [storefast]/[hsfast] the store macros check inline whether a store can be a 60 fps site (pc in the site table or an
  '@address' rule) and whether a write trace is armed; the calls ps2HalfStepWrite / ps2TraceGuestWrite paid on EVERY
  store are gone (same results: those functions returned the value untouched for the others; a fight's state hashes
  are identical to the previous build for 101 points).
- [pacediag] PS2X_PACEDIAG=1: vblank-to-frame latency, frame gaps and the vblank worker's lateness every 5 s.

